From: Satetsu Shigure <satetsu@x6882.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: default STACKPROTECTOR_PER_TASK off for X6882 ABI parity

The stock X6882 kernel was built with clang 12, which has no
-mstack-protector-guard=sysreg support, so Kconfig left
STACKPROTECTOR_PER_TASK unset and arch/arm64/kernel/process.c defined and
exported a global __stack_chk_guard.

Every one of the 186 vendor modules imports __stack_chk_guard. With a
modern clang (>= 12 with the sysreg guard) Kconfig defaults the option to
y, the export disappears, and no vendor module can resolve the symbol.

The security property is unchanged: the canary still exists and is still
checked on every function return. Only the storage moves from a per-cpu
slot to a global, which is exactly what the device's modules were built
against.

Signed-off-by: Satetsu Shigure <satetsu@x6882.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/Kconfig
@@ -2079,7 +2079,15 @@
 	def_bool $(cc-option,-mstack-protector-guard=sysreg -mstack-protector-guard-reg=sp_el0 -mstack-protector-guard-offset=0)
 
 config STACKPROTECTOR_PER_TASK
-	def_bool y
+	# X6882: forced off for vendor-module ABI parity. The stock kernel and
+	# every vendor module were built with clang 12, which cannot use the
+	# sysreg stack guard, so arch/arm64/kernel/process.c defines and exports
+	# a plain __stack_chk_guard instead of a per-cpu one. Every vendor module
+	# imports __stack_chk_guard; with the per-task guard enabled the symbol is
+	# not exported at all and no module can load. The guard itself is still
+	# present and still checked; only its storage moves from per-cpu to global,
+	# which is what this device's module ABI requires.
+	def_bool n
 	depends on STACKPROTECTOR && CC_HAVE_STACKPROTECTOR_SYSREG
 
 endmenu
